      "writtenOn": "2019-11-08T15:30:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "can you add comments to pd_update_try_source (and these functions) that they are called from a different tasks and need to protect access to any state variable.\n\nI looked at drp_state and it looks like the main task only reads from it (instead is access modify write), so we can get away with just making drp_state volatile. The more robust approach would be to cause read and writes to drp_state with a mutex. That would protect us long term if we every changes our read and write patterns in the different tasks.\n\n\nThe same logic apply to the pd_try_src_enable variable since that is accessed in multiple tasks. We should guard access to that via mutex as well.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 361,
        "startChar": 2,
